                            <p>This provenance was listed in MLGB2, with a footnote indicating that
                                the calendar contains the dedication of the church (p. 222).
                                However, no corresponding index card was found during the
                                retroconversion of parish church data in 2026. Compare the following
                                in <bibl>Neil R. Ker, <title>Medieval Manuscripts in British
                                        Libraries</title> (Oxford, 1992), iv, 516:</bibl> 'The
                                entries in art. 1 of the dedication of the church of High Ongar,
                                Essex, and of births and deaths of members of the Walsingham family
                                [...] suggest that the manuscript belonged to the Walsinghams of
                                Scadbury in Kent, who held the manor of Bobbingworth, the next
                                parish to High Ongar'.</p></provenance>
